course: dictionary
lesson: 3545
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it show you which meaning the writer means. Read the context of «feeder» and ask: what is it doing in this sentence? «Squirrels do not hibernate, and they eat buried nuts and seeds from feeders.» Nuts and seeds are eaten from feeders, so a feeder must be something that holds food.
explain: Now read «In parts of North America and Romania bears come into towns for bins, fruit trees and bird feeders.» The bears come for food, so a bird feeder is a container of food, not a bird and not a nest. To check, swap in your meaning: "bears come into towns for bird containers of food" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Feeder can also be a school or a road. In «feeder school», the word school tells you the feeder sends children on to a bigger place. The phrase «feeder road» works the same way: it is a smaller road that joins a bigger one. Always look at the words next to feeder before you decide what it means.
fact: A feeder is a container that holds food for birds or animals.
fact: A feeder school sends pupils on to a bigger secondary school.
fact: A feeder road is a smaller road that joins a bigger road.
fact: A feeder can also be a machine part, like a paper feeder that feeds paper into a printer.
fact: Context clues, such as the words next to a word, help you choose the right meaning when a word has several meanings.
exercise: «Squirrels eat buried nuts and seeds from feeders.» What is a feeder in this sentence? | A bird that sings loudly | A type of tall tree | A squirrel's nest | *A container that holds food
exercise: In school life, what does a feeder school do? | Makes children hungry | Sells books to parents | *Sends pupils on to a bigger school | Cooks lunch for the whole town
exercise: Which phrase uses feeder to mean a smaller road that joins a bigger one? | a night feeder | a messy feeder | a bird feeder | *a feeder road
test: «Bird feeders in the garden help birds in winter.» What does feeders mean here? | A sort of nest | Rivers that run into the sea | *Containers that hold food for birds | A places where birds sleep
test: «Ben is a messy feeder.» What does this mean? | *Ben eats in a messy way | Ben runs a bird feeder shop | Ben cooks for birds in the garden | Ben lives on a feeder road
exam: In «Squirrels eat buried nuts and seeds from feeders», which word is the clue that tells you feeders hold food? | nest | hibernate | squirrels | *nuts
